WEBVTT

00:08:58.476 --> 00:09:00.116
It's not really that threatening.

00:09:00.116 --> 00:09:02.236
It's not something you should fear.

00:09:02.276 --> 00:09:03.516
They're snuffling around,

00:09:03.556 --> 00:09:06.076
they're looking for stuff
and they've got little eyes,

00:09:06.076 --> 00:09:07.436
they're actually gelatinous,

00:09:07.476 --> 00:09:09.956
that's its liver you can see
on the side of its body.

00:09:09.956 --> 00:09:11.156
They're very soft-bodied.

00:09:11.196 --> 00:09:13.956
And what I really love
about the deepest fish in the world

00:09:13.956 --> 00:09:15.676
is they’re not really deep-sea fish.

00:09:15.716 --> 00:09:18.676
They're actually a shallow water family
that has just radiated.

00:09:18.676 --> 00:09:20.716
Most snailfish
are actually really shallow,

00:09:20.756 --> 00:09:22.236
you even get some in estuaries.

00:09:22.276 --> 00:09:25.756
It's just a fish that doesn't care,
you can't pigeonhole the snailfish.

00:09:26.796 --> 00:09:27.916
So ...

00:09:28.596 --> 00:09:32.116
Another animal ... that we
like are prawns, right?